# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF, check them out as LF.
# Keeps `cargo fmt --check` and the CI rustfmt job from disagreeing across OSes.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Named explicitly, not left to the `* text=auto eol=lf` wildcard above.
#
# The scripts in scripts/ are executed directly by CI and by contributors, so a
# CRLF checkout is not cosmetic: bash reads a shebang line containing a stray
# carriage return as part of the interpreter path and fails with "bad
# interpreter". `* text=auto` only applies eol=lf because git can tell these are
# text; being explicit means the requirement survives a future edit to the
# wildcard, and it documents the reason next to the rule.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Keep the license text byte-exact; the Apache appendix spacing matters.
LICENSE text eol=lf

# Binary-ish artifacts that must never be line-ending translated.
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
